          "title": "You'll want to know: ബഹിഷ്കരിക്കുക",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ബഹിഷ്കരിക്കുക — bahiṣkarikkuka — \"to boycott\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിദ്യാർത്ഥികൾ ക്ലാസുകൾ ബഹിഷ്കരിച്ചു. vidyārtthikaḷ klāsukaḷ bahiṣkariccu. The students boycotted classes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past: ബഹിഷ്കരിച്ചു, bahiṣkariccu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun is ബഹിഷ്കരണം, a boycott."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ബഹിഷ്കരിക്കുക (bahiṣkarikkuka) is built from Sanskrit bahiṣkāra, \"expulsion, removal\" (Monier-Williams), from bahis, \"outside\", and kṛ, \"to make\", with the Malayalam verb ending: to put a thing outside."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
